<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ondjiva</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ondjiva is the capital of Cunene Province in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, near the Namibian border. It stands in the former heartland of the Kwanyama kingdom, the most populous of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovambo-people">Ovambo</a> kingdoms, and in the colonial era was named Vila Pereira de Eça. The town was heavily damaged during South African incursions in the Angolan Civil War in the 1980s.</p></div>
